# Defect 416, lane run400, 2026-10-06; found beside defect 400 by the same
# lane.
#
# SYMPTOM: a handle over a union's tag that nothing uses, `heroes test`
# refused with `ffi_tag_is_a_union` (with no test block at all), and `build`
# and `run` wrote and ran the program at exit 0. Each verdict was the other
# verb's contradiction.
#
# CAUSE: `test` compiles the fused unit, which defines every type's per-type
# functions and so spells every group record; `build` compiles one unit per
# module, which spelled only the records that module's code reached. A
# declaration nothing reached was never compiled against its header there.
#
# FIX: each module's unit reaches every group record the module declares
# (`emit/members.hero`'s `group_records`), so every verb asks the header
# about every binding the program writes, as the layout check already did of
# a record with fields: a declaration the header refutes is a mistake in the
# program whether or not a line uses it.

extern "fixedbugs-400-tags-of-three-kinds.h"
    record UH tag utag  #~ ffi_tag_is_a_union

function main()
    print(1)
